Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] DW3_FILE_CACHE_SLOTS test hook: a smaller file cache

findFreeFileSlot (engine/file/file_cache.c) hands out only the first n of the
64 file cache slots when the PC environment has DW3_FILE_CACHE_SLOTS=<n>
(1..63; unset, 0, invalid or 64 mean all of them). The slot count is read once
by dw3_port_file_cache_slots() (port/file_cache/file_cache_host.c), which logs
`dw3-file-cache: DW3_FILE_CACHE_SLOTS=n of 64 (test hook)`. Nothing else uses
the variable: a run without it is identical to main.

Why: on the PS1 the 1.33 MB heap kept the file cache small, and on the host
(8 MiB heap) a long session fills all 64 slots, where requestFile used to write
through a NULL slot (the preview.31-rc1 battle report crash, patch 0096).
Natural play needs about 2 hours to fill the cache (two battles use 46 slots);
the hook makes the same state reachable in one replay. With this patch alone
and a small n the second battle ends in SIGSEGV in requestFile, the owner's
crash; patch 0096 fixes that.

--- a/src/engine/file/file_cache.c
+++ b/src/engine/file/file_cache.c
@@ -2,6 +2,9 @@
 #include <libgs.h>
 #include <libetc.h>
 #include <libsnd.h>
+#if PORT_HOST
+#include "port_file_cache.h"
+#endif
 
 /* The file cache */
 FileCache FILE_CACHE = {
@@ -38,8 +41,14 @@
 FileSlot *findFreeFileSlot(void) {
     FileSlot *slot;
     s32 i;
+#if PORT_HOST
+    /* DW3_FILE_CACHE_SLOTS test hook: hand out only the first n slots */
+    s32 limit = dw3_port_file_cache_slots(FILE_CACHE_SLOTS);
+#else
+    s32 limit = FILE_CACHE_SLOTS;
+#endif
 
-    for (slot = FILE_CACHE.slots, i = 0; i < FILE_CACHE_SLOTS; i++, slot++) {
+    for (slot = FILE_CACHE.slots, i = 0; i < limit; i++, slot++) {
         if (slot->file == 0) {
             return slot;
         }
